==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Coined in 1912 by Swiss psychiatrist {{w|Eugen Bleuler}} (1857-1939) from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|autismus}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|αὐτός||self|sc=polytonic}} + {{m|grc|-ισμός||-ism}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɔːtɪz.əm/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|clinical psychology}} A pervasive [[neurological]] disorder that is observable in early [[childhood]] and persists throughout the lifespan, characterised by atypical communication, language development, eye contact, and sensory experiences.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-29|volume=407|issue=8842|page=72-3|magazine={{w|The Economist}}
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/international/science-and-technology/21580133-how-microbes-promote-liver-cancer-overweight-punch-gut A punch in the gut]
|passage=Mostly, the microbiome is beneficial. It helps with digestion and enables people to extract a lot more calories from their food than would otherwise be possible. Research over the past few years, however, has implicated it in diseases from atherosclerosis to asthma to '''autism'''.}}
# {{lb|en|clinical psychology}} {{synonym of|en|autism spectrum}} (disorder); generalization of the specific to a range.
# {{lb|en|historical|clinical psychology|now medically obsolete}} A diagnosis involving a [[pathological]] tendency to engage in [[self-centered]] [[fantasy]] thinking, historically considered a symptom of [[insanity]] and/or [[schizophrenia]].

